                        "review": "[h1] Experienced on the Oculus Rift with Touch Controllers [/h1]\n\nI bought this in the Steam VR Spring Sale for $2.79 USD. It's not the best bow & arrow VR game, but it's pretty solid and it would be in my top 10 for bow & arrow titles (although probably #9 or #10 on that list). There's just so many good ones, this is a subgenre that is packed with quality titles. The bow feels good. With just a little practice you can snipe things off at a distance and you get bonus gold for being accurate and for headshots. The only odd thing is that the arrow goes on the inside of the bow (right-handed perspective).\n\nSo this is a dark fantasy themed tower defense bow & arrow game. You can teleport all around an area at the top of the tower. You are a female hooded ranger/ queen in disguise and apparently the last defense. There's many types of enemies that try to invade the castle, from wolves to spiders to skeleton warriors, to orcs, to trolls, to flying demons, to shaman. Enemies can attack you and you will have to dodge projectiles. \n\nYou can upgrade your defenses by hiring warriors. You then need to protect from damage or they'll die and it'll be gold lost. You can also upgrade to frost arrows and all kind of other magical arrows. You can also spend coin to repair the castle walls.\n\nI did not get far into the game. I got to Stage 4. Each stage has 4 waves that you have to beat before the next one unlocks. The good thing is that your progress is saved. You have 6 stages to reach the end. I believe there are 2 different environments with 6 stages each. At the end, you get to see where you are on the global leaderboards.\n\nRate 6.5/10. Really solid. Recommended if you're looking for a fantasy themed bow & arrow game. Would have been great with multiplayer.\n\n",
